  "stateNote": "In a 6 qt pot, add grains to 2.25 qts of 168°F water. Mix well to bring the temperature down to 155°F. Steep on stovetop at 155°F for 45 minutes. Meanwhile, bring 2 gallons of water to 165°F in a 12 qt pot. Place strainer over, then pour and spoon all the grains and liquid in. Rinse with 2 gallons of 165°F water. Let liquid drain through. Discard the grains and bring the liquid to a boil. Set aside.",
